WEBVTT

00:14.264 --> 00:16.630
- Chelsea?
Yeah?

00:17.367 --> 00:18.425
You okay?

00:20.770 --> 00:23.466
I think I'm coming down with a cold.

00:27.777 --> 00:32.714
That doesn't sound like a cold.
It sounds like quitting time in Bedrock.

00:32.882 --> 00:34.440
Do I feel hot to you?

00:34.951 --> 00:37.112
- Let me see.
- Stop it.

00:38.054 --> 00:39.521
You're supposed to feel my head.

00:39.923 --> 00:42.187
Yeah, but those babies
are my frame of reference.

00:44.794 --> 00:48.161
- Maybe I should go home.
- If you think that's the right thing to do.

00:48.331 --> 00:52.131
Charlie, it's the middle of the night
and I'm sick. I'm not going home.

00:52.869 --> 00:55.531
- Then why did you say you were?
- I was testing you.

00:56.439 --> 01:00.170
Yeah, well, I knew that,
and I was testing you.

01:00.343 --> 01:02.470
I think we both did very well.

01:05.949 --> 01:08.509
Tell you what,
you get a good night's sleep.

01:08.685 --> 01:11.745
- I'm sure you'll feel better in the morning.
- Where are you going?

01:12.222 --> 01:15.157
I'm gonna crash on the couch,
let you have the whole bed to yourself.

01:15.558 --> 01:17.423
Really?
You're gonna leave me here alone?

01:18.094 --> 01:21.655
No, no. I just thought
you might want your own space.

01:22.298 --> 01:25.233
You know, when dogs are sick,
they hide till they feel better.

01:27.704 --> 01:30.332
Probably why they're man's best friend.

01:31.207 --> 01:32.606
Could you please stay?

01:35.111 --> 01:36.339
Pretty please?

01:38.047 --> 01:39.446
How can I say no?

01:41.584 --> 01:43.779
Seriously, how?

01:44.821 --> 01:46.846
Spoon?

01:49.392 --> 01:51.519
Try and stop me.

02:04.107 --> 02:06.598
So, what,
are you just gonna swallow that?

02:06.876 --> 02:08.867
Go to sleep.

02:17.687 --> 02:19.052
What are you doing?

02:19.222 --> 02:22.350
Come on, you know what happens
when we spoon.

02:22.525 --> 02:24.322
I'm sick.

02:24.494 --> 02:26.894
Obviously so am I.

02:28.364 --> 02:29.729
All right, fine.

02:31.601 --> 02:33.262
Go ahead.

02:36.840 --> 02:39.434
This is another test, isn't it?

03:08.738 --> 03:11.229
&lt;i>Coming up next
on Turner Classic Movies:&lt;/i>

03:11.407 --> 03:14.205
&lt;i>The Bridges of Madison County.&lt;/i>

03:17.447 --> 03:19.574
I am not gonna cry.

03:22.018 --> 03:23.246
Hey.

03:23.753 --> 03:24.777
What are you doing up?

03:25.355 --> 03:27.550
Watching a Clint Eastwood movie.

03:30.827 --> 03:31.851
What are you doing up?

03:32.262 --> 03:33.593
Chelsea's sick.

03:33.763 --> 03:36.197
She was coughing and sneezing
all over the place.

03:36.366 --> 03:37.390
Oh, no.

03:37.567 --> 03:39.967
Yeah. I had to wait
until she finally fell asleep...

03:40.136 --> 03:42.798
...so I could get out of there
without pissing her off.

03:43.273 --> 03:44.433
How considerate.

03:45.975 --> 03:49.411
What do you want from me?
I'm not a big phlegm fan.

03:51.748 --> 03:55.047
- This isn't a Clint Eastwood movie.
- Yes, it is.

03:55.718 --> 03:58.915
Even Clint Eastwood doesn't think
this is a Clint Eastwood movie.

03:59.088 --> 04:00.385
Well, tough. I like it.

04:00.556 --> 04:03.389
Sure you do.
You're a giant fruit basket.

04:03.559 --> 04:05.891
I'll never apologize for my feminine side.

04:09.832 --> 04:11.356
Boy, I hope she gets better soon.

04:11.534 --> 04:13.968
This sick stuff
is not what I signed on for.

04:15.939 --> 04:19.841
You're kidding, right?
This is exactly what you signed on for.

04:21.244 --> 04:24.372
You told Chelsea you loved her.
You gave her an engagement ring.

04:24.547 --> 04:27.675
This is what it's all about,
being there for her no matter what.

04:27.850 --> 04:30.842
For richer or poorer, better or worse,
in sickness and in health.

04:31.454 --> 04:36.084
Call me crazy,
but I prefer richer, better and health.

04:37.293 --> 04:39.989
Well, regardless,
this could be a real opportunity for you.

04:40.930 --> 04:43.421
Opportunity for what,
a massive infection?

04:43.933 --> 04:46.493
An opportunity to show her
that she can depend on you...

04:46.669 --> 04:48.933
...that you're not just there
for the good times.

04:49.105 --> 04:51.300
Okay, I hear that.

04:51.474 --> 04:53.101
- Tell me one thing.
- Yeah?

04:53.276 --> 04:54.834
What's in it for me?

04:57.046 --> 04:59.139
Watch Clint and Meryl.

04:59.515 --> 05:01.176
Learn how to love.

05:06.022 --> 05:09.014
I'll take my chances in the snot locker.

05:14.230 --> 05:16.323
I will not cry.

05:20.937 --> 05:22.962
Charlie?

05:24.407 --> 05:26.398
You awake?

05:42.225 --> 05:44.250
Boy, I hope not.

05:45.762 --> 05:47.753
I feel awful.

05:48.231 --> 05:49.823
Really?

05:50.199 --> 05:52.030
You look swell.

05:52.602 --> 05:53.694
I should go home.

05:53.870 --> 05:57.203
No, no, no.
I am not falling for that again.

05:57.373 --> 05:59.933
You stay right here,
let me take care of you.

06:00.109 --> 06:02.339
You mean it?

06:02.512 --> 06:04.878
Oh, man.
Do I have to mean it too?

06:06.582 --> 06:09.415
Just kidding.
Can I make you some tea or something?

06:09.585 --> 06:12.179
- Yes, please.
- Coming up.

06:12.355 --> 06:15.256
- With honey.
- Sure.

06:15.425 --> 06:17.188
And maybe an English muffin.

06:18.628 --> 06:19.890
No problem.

06:20.063 --> 06:21.223
Toasted crispy.

06:23.833 --> 06:24.857
Right.

06:25.034 --> 06:27.901
And let the butter melt
into all the nooks and crannies...

06:28.071 --> 06:29.629
...before you put the jam on.

06:31.741 --> 06:33.208
Anything else?

06:33.376 --> 06:35.435
Can I have a hug?

06:42.118 --> 06:43.380
Try and stop me.

06:56.399 --> 06:58.299
- Nice necklace.
- Thanks.

06:58.468 --> 07:01.164
- Buy it for yourself?
- No, a girl gave it to me.

07:02.138 --> 07:04.072
Really? She must like you.

07:04.240 --> 07:06.800
Yeah, she's nuts for me.

07:06.976 --> 07:10.468
- Well, is she cute?
- I guess.

07:11.013 --> 07:13.607
- You don't seem very happy about it.
- I'm not.

07:14.550 --> 07:17.314
- Why, what's the problem?
- She's nine.

07:20.823 --> 07:23.257
Nine? Where would you meet
a nine-year-old girl?

07:23.726 --> 07:25.990
We're in the same math class.

07:27.864 --> 07:29.855
Is, uh-
Is she one of those advanced students?

07:30.366 --> 07:31.799
Sadly no.

07:33.336 --> 07:35.167
But she does help me
with my homework.

07:37.807 --> 07:39.604
Hey, Berta.

07:39.775 --> 07:43.006
Chelsea's not feeling well.
Could you make her tea and English muffin?

07:43.446 --> 07:44.606
Sure, I could.

07:48.251 --> 07:50.048
But you won't.

07:50.219 --> 07:52.050
Is that what you're saying?

07:54.557 --> 07:57.958
- Where are the muffins?
- In the fridge, as always.

07:58.461 --> 07:59.985
Don't condescend to me.

08:00.663 --> 08:03.063
He does it to me all the time.
It's very irritating.

08:03.866 --> 08:04.958
No one's talking to you.

08:05.134 --> 08:06.362
See? Like that.

08:06.536 --> 08:08.003
That wasn't condescending.

08:08.171 --> 08:09.638
But that was, right?

08:10.840 --> 08:12.432
Right.

08:13.409 --> 08:15.877
Boy, as soon as I get my license,
I am so out of here.

08:16.045 --> 08:19.412
Sure. You can drive your girlfriend
to Gymboree.

08:20.216 --> 08:21.740
At least I have a girlfriend.

08:25.388 --> 08:27.219
"At least I have a girlfriend."

08:29.525 --> 08:31.755
So, what's the deal?
Does, uh, Chelsea have a cold?

08:31.928 --> 08:35.420
Not sure. Cold, flu.
Something disgusting.

08:36.632 --> 08:38.327
Maybe she has an STD.

08:39.335 --> 08:42.236
- What?
- I mean sexually transmitted disease.

08:42.672 --> 08:44.333
I know what STD's are.

08:44.840 --> 08:46.273
Your uncle helped invent them.

08:49.879 --> 08:52.404
You know they can be prevented
by using a condom.

08:52.582 --> 08:55.551
I know we could've prevented you
by using a condom.

08:57.253 --> 08:59.221
Now we gotta use a hammer.

09:00.856 --> 09:01.880
I don't understand.

09:02.058 --> 09:04.390
Go get me a hammer and I'll show you.

09:06.229 --> 09:07.594
Okay.

09:10.733 --> 09:12.428
You must be so proud.

09:13.803 --> 09:16.397
Ballpeen or claw hammer?

09:17.773 --> 09:21.265
Do me a favor.
When he comes back, just do it.

09:24.146 --> 09:27.707
Okay. Here we go. Room service.

09:29.352 --> 09:31.616
Chelsea? Honey?

09:31.787 --> 09:35.279
Don't come in.
- Wasn't even tempted.

09:37.159 --> 09:38.888
I got your tea and muffins.

09:39.061 --> 09:43.191
Oh, I have diarrhea. I can't eat now.

09:43.799 --> 09:45.426
I may never eat again.

09:46.936 --> 09:49.268
Would you mind going
to the drugstore for me?

09:50.006 --> 09:52.770
For you, I'd go to the ends of the earth.

09:52.942 --> 09:55.706
Coming back's a whole other question.

09:56.212 --> 09:59.477
What?
- I said what do you need?

09:59.649 --> 10:03.176
Well, I need Pepto and we're
almost out of tissues.

10:03.352 --> 10:06.879
And I need some decongestant,
some cough syrup...

10:07.056 --> 10:10.321
...something for canker sores
and wet wipes.

10:10.493 --> 10:11.721
For your hands?

10:11.894 --> 10:13.953
- No.
- Got it.

10:16.098 --> 10:19.295
And I'm probably gonna need
some tampons.

10:19.468 --> 10:22.562
Oh, great. There's gonna be blood too.

10:23.973 --> 10:27.374
You're really being wonderful
about all this, Charlie.

10:27.543 --> 10:30.979
Oh, It's nothing. It's what a guy does
when he loves somebody.

10:32.615 --> 10:33.980
Ah. Should have known.

10:34.150 --> 10:37.916
The second you give them a ring
they fall out of warranty.

10:46.796 --> 10:48.559
- Hey, Russell.
- Mm-hm.

10:48.731 --> 10:51.894
- What's good for canker sores?
- You got canker sores?

10:52.068 --> 10:53.092
No. My girlfriend.

10:53.703 --> 10:56.433
- What do you recommend?
- Tennis shoes.

10:57.206 --> 10:59.936
- Excuse me?
- Put them on and run away.

11:00.109 --> 11:02.600
There's a lot of broads out there.
Find a clean one.

11:05.548 --> 11:08.108
I can't run away.
I'm kind of engaged to her.

11:08.284 --> 11:10.752
Oh, Charlie. No.

11:10.920 --> 11:12.512
Yep, I bit the bullet.

11:13.890 --> 11:15.050
You bit the big one.

11:15.992 --> 11:19.428
Hey, just because you blew three marriages
doesn't mean I can't make this work.

11:21.397 --> 11:23.058
You're a funny guy, Charlie.

11:23.232 --> 11:25.826
And that's not just
the OxyContin talking.

11:27.203 --> 11:30.297
Here you go. Cank Be Gone.

11:30.473 --> 11:33.340
- What else?
- Ah, let's see. Cough syrup.

11:33.509 --> 11:36.740
- Regular or codeine?
- Don't you need a prescription for codeine?

11:36.913 --> 11:38.505
What are you, a cop?

11:40.817 --> 11:44.116
Here. I'll give you the kid stuff.

11:44.287 --> 11:45.345
What else?

11:45.521 --> 11:49.514
Uh, tissues, throat lozenges, decongestant,
Pepto, wet wipes.

11:50.059 --> 11:53.551
Jeez, where did you find this one,
a hospital parking lot?

11:54.063 --> 11:55.462
Come on, Russell. Help me out.

11:55.631 --> 11:57.622
Okay. Okay. Here you go.

11:59.001 --> 12:01.868
A dam for every river...

12:02.038 --> 12:04.734
...a plug for every jug.

12:05.975 --> 12:08.569
Oh, right. I almost forgot.
She also needs tampons.

12:08.744 --> 12:10.041
Oh, lucky you.

12:11.514 --> 12:12.538
What size?

12:13.416 --> 12:15.281
How should I know?

12:15.585 --> 12:19.851
Is there some kind of a condom-tampon
conversion chart?

12:20.556 --> 12:22.581
No. But that's an amusing idea.

12:23.960 --> 12:28.329
Actually, it's not about size per se,
it's more about flow.

12:29.165 --> 12:33.226
See, that's a piece of information I could've
gone the rest of my life without knowing.

12:34.704 --> 12:37.036
Here you go. Here's a variety pack.

12:37.206 --> 12:41.074
This will handle anything
from a little drizzle to a monsoon.

12:43.246 --> 12:46.113
Listen, is it too late
to change my mind about the codeine?

12:49.886 --> 12:51.945
The first one's free.

12:52.121 --> 12:53.349
&lt;i>Thank you.&lt;/i>

13:02.999 --> 13:04.125
Okay.

13:04.300 --> 13:05.358
Got all of your stuff.

13:05.534 --> 13:06.694
Took you long enough.

13:06.869 --> 13:10.669
Whoa, whoa, I just went shopping
from wet wipes and tampons.

13:10.840 --> 13:12.569
I'm allowed to take my time.

13:13.075 --> 13:14.565
Sorry. You mad at me?

13:15.177 --> 13:17.873
No. No. Why would I be mad at you?

13:18.047 --> 13:20.641
Because I'm sick
and you have to take care of me.

13:22.018 --> 13:24.953
Are you kidding me?
I love taking care of you.

13:25.121 --> 13:27.089
I just love...

13:29.191 --> 13:30.818
...it.

13:30.993 --> 13:33.223
Yeah, I can see that.

13:33.663 --> 13:35.062
Listen.

13:35.231 --> 13:39.099
Can you go over to my place and get me
some clean clothes and feed Sir Lancelot?

13:39.936 --> 13:41.563
- Who?
- My cat.

13:43.239 --> 13:45.298
He's not gonna feed himself, Charlie.

13:45.474 --> 13:47.999
Are you sure? Maybe you've got mice.

13:48.444 --> 13:51.277
Oh, you're probably gonna have
to change the litter box too.

13:52.348 --> 13:54.441
Change it into what?

13:55.017 --> 13:57.918
You got to scoop out the poop
and put in fresh litter.

13:58.721 --> 14:01.849
Oh, this just keeps getting better
and better.

14:02.391 --> 14:03.585
Charlie.

14:03.759 --> 14:06.023
- Yeah?
- I love you.

14:06.495 --> 14:08.122
Great.

14:08.664 --> 14:09.995
Aren't you gonna say it back?

14:11.400 --> 14:13.425
I'm gonna go pan for cat turds.

14:14.837 --> 14:17.431
If that doesn't say I love you,
nothing does.

14:20.242 --> 14:22.608
I promise, I'm wearing it.

14:22.778 --> 14:24.473
Wait a sec.

14:28.284 --> 14:29.911
Okay, I sent you a picture.

14:30.086 --> 14:31.917
Now what's the answer to number four?

14:32.088 --> 14:33.851
Oh, yeah, that's what I had.

14:37.893 --> 14:39.451
- What you doing Alan?
- My taxes.

14:39.628 --> 14:42.153
I promised myself I wouldn't wait
till the last minute.

14:42.331 --> 14:45.129
Yeah, you promised me
you'd only stay here for a few days...

14:45.301 --> 14:46.700
...so your word means nothing.

14:48.337 --> 14:50.999
- You're driving me to Chelsea's.
- Why don't you drive yourself?

14:51.173 --> 14:53.573
Because I just chugged
a half a bottle of codeine...

14:53.743 --> 14:57.338
...and this bourbon might make me
a bit of a threat on the road.

14:58.014 --> 14:59.982
Ah, good call.

15:02.752 --> 15:03.980
Here kitty, kitty.

15:05.321 --> 15:07.380
Here kitty, kitty, kitty.

15:07.556 --> 15:09.683
Okay, I got her clean clothes.

15:09.859 --> 15:13.488
Great.
Now I just gotta feed the damn cat.

15:13.662 --> 15:15.857
Come on, Sir Lancelot.

15:16.032 --> 15:17.624
Come out and eat your kibble.

15:19.201 --> 15:20.361
Ow!

15:20.970 --> 15:23.234
Son of a bitch.

15:23.406 --> 15:27.570
I'm pretty sure if you just put the food out,
he'll find it and eat it when he's hungry.

15:27.743 --> 15:29.574
Really? Think if he was that smart...

15:29.745 --> 15:32.339
...he'd just crap in the toilet
instead of a litter box.

15:33.182 --> 15:34.877
Oh, uh, did you change the litter yet?

15:35.618 --> 15:38.086
No, I was actually gonna
offer you $20 to do it.

15:38.788 --> 15:40.813
I'll take it. Ha, ha.

15:40.990 --> 15:42.116
Deal.

15:42.291 --> 15:44.623
Ha, ha. I would have done it for 10.

15:44.794 --> 15:46.728
Ha, ha.
I would have given you a thousand.

15:51.333 --> 15:52.425
Whoa.

15:52.601 --> 15:54.330
Big cat.

15:56.238 --> 15:57.899
You know what I just realized, Alan?

15:58.340 --> 16:00.808
Cough syrup and hard liquor don't mix?

16:01.744 --> 16:03.905
No, they're delightful.

16:05.014 --> 16:08.211
I'm thinking sooner or later Chelsea's
gonna wanna move in with me.

16:08.384 --> 16:11.683
Yeah, you marry her
that's the chance you take.

16:13.155 --> 16:16.522
And she's probably gonna
wanna bring Sir Craps-A-Lot.

16:18.060 --> 16:19.254
You never know.

16:19.428 --> 16:21.760
He might want to get his own place.

16:22.665 --> 16:24.929
I'm guessing he will before you will.

16:25.868 --> 16:27.096
Oh, Lord.

16:27.269 --> 16:29.169
This cat's been eating more than kibble.

16:29.905 --> 16:32.203
This turd's got feathers.

16:35.344 --> 16:37.437
You know there's a real chance
that someday...

16:37.613 --> 16:39.604
...without any kind of warning
whatsoever...

16:39.782 --> 16:42.012
...Chelsea will up and decide
to get sick again.

16:42.551 --> 16:45.987
We're on the air with codeine and bourbon.
Go ahead caller.

16:47.056 --> 16:49.388
I'm just saying I don't think
I can go through it again.

16:49.558 --> 16:51.150
I'm not cut out to be a caregiver.

16:51.327 --> 16:53.386
Ah, you might not think so
but you're doing it.

16:53.562 --> 16:56.827
You, Charlie Harper, are unselfishly
taking care of the woman you love.

16:57.833 --> 16:59.425
Maybe so, but, uh...

16:59.602 --> 17:01.593
...it's getting harder and harder
to love her.

17:01.770 --> 17:03.135
You don't mean that.

17:03.305 --> 17:08.800
Oh, Alan, if you'd seen and heard
the things I have in the last 24 hours...

17:08.978 --> 17:11.674
...it'd turn you gayer
than a French horn.

17:12.781 --> 17:15.045
Excuse me,
but I have witnessed childbirth.

17:15.217 --> 17:16.741
I saw my son's enormous head...

17:16.919 --> 17:19.786
...poke out of what used to be
one of my very favorite places.

17:21.357 --> 17:23.325
Thanks for the image.

17:23.492 --> 17:27.485
I'll never be able to watch
the kid pull on a sweater again.

17:27.663 --> 17:32.066
If you hang in there, show Chelsea you'll
stick by her even when not at her best...

17:32.268 --> 17:36.102
...she will love you more deeply and
intensely than you could have imagined.

17:36.272 --> 17:37.398
And you know this how?

17:37.840 --> 17:38.898
How else? Chick flicks.

17:41.177 --> 17:44.476
Oh, this is not a kitty cat.

17:44.647 --> 17:47.081
This is a mountain lion.

17:47.550 --> 17:50.018
- Look.
- Hey, hey, hey.

18:00.763 --> 18:03.698
- You need some more orange juice?
- No, thank you.

18:03.866 --> 18:06.733
It was so nice of you to bring some up
without me even asking.

18:07.169 --> 18:08.761
Don't tell Charlie.

18:08.938 --> 18:12.237
It's taken a long time to train him
not to expect anything from me.

18:13.142 --> 18:14.666
Got it.

18:16.946 --> 18:18.573
He really is crazy about you, you know.

18:18.747 --> 18:21.477
- You think?
- Are you kidding?

18:21.650 --> 18:23.277
Charlie doesn't go near sick women.

18:23.719 --> 18:26.187
I mean, physically sick.

18:26.388 --> 18:27.514
Around here...

18:27.690 --> 18:31.626
...one sneeze will get you a cab fare
and a complimentary travel mug.

18:32.895 --> 18:35.420
I have noticed he's trying very hard.

18:35.598 --> 18:40.729
Just remember, when it comes to nurturing,
Charlie's like a dog playing the piano.

18:40.903 --> 18:43.269
You can't fault him
if he hits a few bum notes.

18:43.806 --> 18:47.640
You just got to applaud the effort
and hope he doesn't whiz all over the keys.

18:49.211 --> 18:50.405
I understand.

18:51.647 --> 18:53.547
Thanks, Berta.

18:56.185 --> 18:58.050
Just so we're clear this ain't no hotel.

18:58.220 --> 19:00.415
You need more towels
you get them yourself.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.652
Sorry about that.

19:06.829 --> 19:08.592
You really can't expect much from her.

19:09.398 --> 19:10.490
I won't.

19:11.267 --> 19:13.963
Here. I got you clean clothes
and underwear.

19:15.304 --> 19:19.104
The cat's fed
and the litter box is turd free.

19:19.275 --> 19:20.469
Thank you, Charlie.

19:20.643 --> 19:23.009
You have been so wonderful
through all of this.

19:23.178 --> 19:25.646
I have, haven't I?

19:27.016 --> 19:28.881
I just want you to know...

19:29.051 --> 19:31.281
...I am definitely
gonna make it up to you.

19:31.787 --> 19:35.018
Chelsea, to be honest,
that's the only thing that's kept me going.

19:37.259 --> 19:39.193
- Uh-oh.
- Uh-oh, what?

19:47.169 --> 19:49.160
Oh, Charlie, I'm so sorry.

19:49.605 --> 19:51.232
No, no. It's okay.

19:51.407 --> 19:52.806
At least it's not wicker.

19:55.311 --> 19:57.108
Excuse me a second.

20:17.666 --> 20:21.659
Okay, I am going to go to the pharmacy
and get your medicine.

20:21.837 --> 20:24.772
If you get it from Russell, count the pills.

20:25.541 --> 20:27.133
Will do.

20:27.576 --> 20:30.044
- Hope you feel better.
- Thanks.

20:30.212 --> 20:32.737
Charlie, you don't mind
Sir Lancelot being here, do you?

20:32.915 --> 20:34.439
No. Not at all.

20:34.616 --> 20:37.084
- I love cats.
- Good.

20:44.426 --> 20:47.418
Don't scratch the door, Sir Lancelot.

20:52.368 --> 20:53.801
Clean my litter box?

20:53.969 --> 20:56.028
Oh, come on. I've been sick.

20:56.605 --> 20:59.301
Fine. I'll just use your facilities.

20:59.742 --> 21:01.869
Not in the tub this time, okay?

21:03.312 --> 21:05.212
Your house, your rules.

21:11.920 --> 21:13.251
I'm not going to make it.

21:15.491 --> 21:17.618
Yes, you are.
